Validate and decode forward_type=gloss models with the training-time gloss input.

Applies to: Atrewin/SignXmDA b6e2ca4ea81cab41cf858e1d0ce948a778cb09a5
Used by: the conditional teacher runs only (gate teacher-gloss-decoding,
resolved as patch-mirror-training by the assignee on 2026-10-29).

INVENTED BEHAVIOR CHOICE. In training, Batch_Sign repeats every gloss by
ratio = sum(sgn_lengths) // sum(gls_lengths) (min 1) and exposes
gls_input_mask / gls_input_lengths, which get_loss_for_batch(gloss) reads.
The plain Batch built by prediction_XmDA for validation and test has no such
fields, so validating a forward_type=gloss model raises AttributeError
('Batch' object has no attribute 'gls_input_mask'; run
preflight-phoenix14t-teacher), and run_batch(gloss) feeds un-repeated
glosses. This patch makes Batch build the gloss input exactly as Batch_Sign
does, using the sign lengths present in every split, and makes
run_batch(gloss) use the repeated input, mask and lengths, consistent with
get_loss_for_batch. The authors' development fork Atrewin/slt commit
9ecb427b159de5aaaa6bd21a5957f74d752564c1 ("all extend gloss") added the
repetition to the training batch classes and get_loss_for_batch and left
Batch and run_batch without it, so no author evidence shows how, or whether,
this path was ever decoded.

Scope: Batch is only constructed in prediction_XmDA (validation and test) by
the training_XmDA entry point, and run_batch is only called there, so the
training path is unchanged. gls, gls_lengths and gls_mask keep their values;
the sign path (forward_type sign, all baselines) reads none of the changed
fields.

diff --git a/signjoey/batch.py b/signjoey/batch.py
index 88365d5..7fe1d91 100644
--- a/signjoey/batch.py
+++ b/signjoey/batch.py
@@ -113,12 +113,15 @@ class Batch:
             #self.num_gls_tokens = gls_lengths.sum().detach().clone().numpy()
             # @jinhui
 
-            self.gls_input = gls
+            ratio = int(max(torch.sum(self.sgn_lengths)// torch.sum(gls_lengths), 1))
+            self.gls_input = gls.repeat_interleave(ratio, dim=1)
+            self.gls_input_lengths = gls_lengths * ratio
+            self.gls_input_mask = (self.gls_input != gla_pad_index).unsqueeze(1)
             self.gls_lengths = gls_lengths
 
             self.gls = gls
             # we exclude the padded areas from the loss computation
-            self.gls_mask = (self.gls_input != gla_pad_index).unsqueeze(1)
+            self.gls_mask = (self.gls != gla_pad_index).unsqueeze(1)
             self.num_gls_tokens = (self.gls != gla_pad_index).data.sum().item()
 
         if use_cuda:
@@ -142,6 +145,7 @@ class Batch:
             self.gls = self.gls.cuda()
             self.gls_mask = self.gls_mask.cuda()
             self.gls_input = self.gls_input.cuda()
+            self.gls_input_mask = self.gls_input_mask.cuda()
 
     def sort_by_sgn_lengths(self):
         """
@@ -167,6 +171,8 @@ class Batch:
 
             self.gls_mask = self.gls_mask[perm_index]
             self.gls_input = self.gls_input[perm_index]
+            self.gls_input_mask = self.gls_input_mask[perm_index]
+            self.gls_input_lengths = self.gls_input_lengths[perm_index]
 
         if self.txt is not None:
             self.txt = self.txt[perm_index]
